The workspace was inspected, a cleaning script was created and run, and `output.json` was generated.

```json
[
  {
    "email": "alice@example.com",
    "signup": "2024-01-20",
    "score": 88
  },
  {
    "email": "bob@mail.net",
    "signup": "2024-02-15",
    "score": 91
  },
  {
    "email": "carol@site.org",
    "signup": "2024-03-02",
    "score": 77
  },
  {
    "email": "frank@shop.co",
    "signup": "2024-06-11",
    "score": 64
  },
  {
    "email": "gina@lab.ai",
    "signup": "2024-07-07",
    "score": 70
  }
]
```

Invalid rows (`dave-at-nowhere` no `@`, `erin@works.io` empty score, empty email) were dropped, emails lower-cased, dates normalized from `DD/MM/YYYY` to `YYYY-MM-DD`, duplicates merged keeping the highest score per email, and the remaining records are sorted by email ascending. The result is written to `output.json`.
